==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|profound|alt1=prof(o)und|ity}}, from {{uder|en|fro|profundite}}, from {{uder|en|la|profunditās}}. Compare {{m|en|profoundness}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|prəfŭn′dĭtē}}, {{IPA|en|/pɹəˈfʌndɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-profundity.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|pro|fun|di|ty}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪti|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The state of being [[profound]] or [[abstruse]].
# A [[great]] [[depth]].
# [[deep|Deep]] [[intellect]] or [[insight]].

